    "short_description": "The University of South Africa (UNISA) is the largest higher education institution in South Africa and a leader in distance education globally. Established in 1873, it became the first public university to offer education entirely through distance learning in 1946. UNISA is a public, non-profit institution funded by the South African government, with its headquarters in Pretoria and a network of regional hubs across the country and internationally.\n\nUNISA offers a wide range of internationally accredited academic programs at undergraduate and postgraduate levels across various fields, including accounting, education, law, and science. The university employs Open Distance Learning (ODL) and e-learning methodologies, allowing students to study flexibly from anywhere. With an enrollment of approximately 370,000 to 420,000 students from over 130 countries, UNISA serves a diverse audience, including working professionals, remote residents, and marginalized communities. Its mission is to provide accessible education and foster lifelong learning, contributing to the development of individuals and society.",
